WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.290
- All right, y'all know I
always like to end the hour

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.930
with something fun and
different from social media.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.800
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.980
(upbeat music plays and audience cheers)

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.077
So today we've been
celebrating awesome couples,

00:00:10.077 --> 00:00:11.794
so I want to share an
incredible love story

00:00:11.794 --> 00:00:15.064
more than 50 years in
the making, it's a movie.

00:00:15.064 --> 00:00:18.330
It starts back in North Carolina in 1964

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.522
when then-high-schoolers
Vivian and Jim started dating,

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:23.040
so cute!

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.930
For two years, they were inseparable,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.910
that is, until Jim had
to move to New Jersey

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.260
to care for his mom.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.260
It was another two years before
they'd see each other again

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.230
for one whirlwind visit, okay.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.945
After which, fine, they lost touch.

00:00:36.945 --> 00:00:40.530
Their lives went on individually,
each getting married.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.660
Jim had a successful radio career,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.430
but they never forgot about one another.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.915
And finally in 2020, they reconnected,

00:00:46.915 --> 00:00:50.294
and late last year, they
became husband and wife.

00:00:50.294 --> 00:00:51.427
(audience cheering)

00:00:51.427 --> 00:00:54.630
- [Kelly] But there's
even more to the story!

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.300
We have Vivian and Jim on
the line to share it all.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.360
They watch on ABC 45 Greensboro.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.193
Hi, y'all!

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.403
- Kelly!

00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:07.867
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, so...
- Hello, how are you?

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.810
- Thank you so much for being on the show.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.880
I love, this is like a movie, your story.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.250
So, how did you lose touch?

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.910
- Well, I lost touch when my
mom became ill in New Jersey.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.250
I went back to take care of her,

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.050
but I thought I was gonna only be gone

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.640
for a couple of months,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.210
and I ended up staying and
finishing school in New Jersey.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.703
- We did, I did visit
him for a short while,

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.640
so a few years before,

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.060
and I had to get back to North Carolina.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.310
I went to New Jersey to visit him,

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.770
and I had to get back to North Carolina,

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:45.009
and shortly after that, I
realized that I was pregnant

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:47.516
with Jim's daughter.

00:01:47.516 --> 00:01:48.349
- What?

00:01:48.349 --> 00:01:50.842
- I went back to New Jersey to tell Jim.

00:01:50.842 --> 00:01:53.490
But he wasn't there.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.740
He had moved, and I didn't know it.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.310
He had moved to Maryland
to pursue his radio career,

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.500
but I didn't know that at the time.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.867
So I always said, I
always thought to myself,

00:02:04.867 --> 00:02:08.730
"He will find me. One
day he will find me."

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:13.200
And I kept that belief
in my head for 50 years.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.490
And it came true.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.551
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:16.551 --> 00:02:18.000
(audience applauding)

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.350
So how did you reconnect,
and what was that like?

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.840
And then like, you have a kid.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.670
- Well, I actually
reconnected with a friend

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.769
after retiring from radio.

00:02:28.769 --> 00:02:30.570
He asked me what I was gonna do,

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.270
and I said "Well, I might like to connect

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.370
with my high school sweetheart again."

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.304
He said, "What's her name?"

00:02:36.304 --> 00:02:38.040
And I told him the name,

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:41.987
and he looked it up on
Facebook and found her,

00:02:41.987 --> 00:02:44.370
and he said "Oh, she's gorgeous!"

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:45.900
And he said, "Okay, I'll send it to you,

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.120
and let me know if it's the same lady."

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.480
And I said "Oh my gosh, she
is gorgeous! That's her!"

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.700
He said, "Let me do some more information,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.191
find out some more information about her,

00:02:55.191 --> 00:02:57.300
and I'll get back to you."

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.070
- Oh my gosh, I love this story.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.240
Go ahead, Vivian.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.400
- And he did, he found me,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.550
and I invited this young man to dinner.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.252
I had to see him for myself and touch him

00:03:08.252 --> 00:03:10.233
to make sure this is for real.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.690
And I invited him to dinner,

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.940
he came over, and he stood at that door,

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.070
I opened that door and
he was standing there,

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.230
I was so excited, my heart was beating,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.100
I just reached and snatched him in

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.266
and hugged him and kissed him.

00:03:23.266 --> 00:03:24.099
- Aw.

00:03:25.401 --> 00:03:27.653
Aw, I love this story!

00:03:27.653 --> 00:03:30.270
- I was really excited,
I couldn't help myself!

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.610
- Well, 50 years, you
at least deserve a hug,

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:33.860
I'm just sayin', like....

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:40.593
Like, at least. You're due something!

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.180
- It was exciting, oh my, it was exciting.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.040
My heart was beating so fast,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.972
and Jim was standing there,

00:03:48.972 --> 00:03:53.040
and with that voice, oh
my gracious, that voice,

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.410
he's talking about "Hello, Vivian,"

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:58.170
and there's the voice I didn't recognize,

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.610
but I loved it.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:03.000
He just turned my head all the way around.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.090
- Oh my gosh, I love you two so much.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:09.788
This should be a movie, and
y'all should star in it.

00:04:09.788 --> 00:04:11.490
Oh my God, I love y'all so much.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:14.070
Thank you so much Vivian,
thank you so much Jim.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.573
I'm liking your post right now.

00:04:15.573 --> 00:04:19.105
(audience cheering)

00:04:19.105 --> 00:04:21.180
And that's not all!

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:22.530
Wait one second, that's not all.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.990
Our season-long partner Pilot
Pen, makers of Friction,

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.790
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.610
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly,

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.277
just like y'all, I mean,
creating for 50 years, ma'am.

00:04:32.277 --> 00:04:35.642
So they're giving you
$1000, how's that sound?

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:39.725
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.676
Oh my gosh, y'all have so
much fun with that money!

